# Line endings.
#
# This repo is authored on Windows and runs on Linux. Git's autocrlf checked shell scripts out with
# CRLF, so `#!/usr/bin/env bash` became `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` on the server and the kernel looked
# for an interpreter literally named "bash\r". The nightly backup was scheduled, appeared installed,
# and had never once produced a file.
#
# Anything with a shebang, or read by a Linux tool, is forced to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
*.bash      text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.sql       text eol=lf

# Windows-only helpers keep CRLF, since that is what their interpreters expect.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf

# Never touched.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.gz        binary
*.cer       binary
